Z||000000||Will||12-02-2001||11:08 AM||||Jay, Northstar87, artherd, or anyone else who has the resources, can you post picutres of exactly what has to be done to the right side decklid hinge and the right strut tower to put a N* in a Fiero without moving it left?<BR>For the hinge, I think that a picture taken through the quarter window, and/or a picture taken from the left side of the engine bay so that I can see how the cam cover interferes with the outline of the hinge body would be good.<BR>For the strut tower, just take a picture of what's dented/cut away/welded back.<P>Many Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||12-03-2001||03:04 AM||||Hi Will, I'm afraid I've only done one test-fit, and that was withought the front mount finished, so I can't say.<P>But on the 88 the strut tower looks like it pretty much clears.  The hinge basically gets it's bottom half cut away... (I am going to weld in some reinforcing before it all goes back together, just in case(TM)<P>Realise this dosen't help much...<P>Also, here's a Northstar related question; what exactly do the little coolant system tablets that GM wants added when coolant is changed, actually DO?!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
